      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider each item in the entrees, drinks, and desserts columns and calculate the total number of combinations.\n\n1. **Identify the number of choices for each category:**\n   - Entrees: There are 4 options (Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, Fish and Chips).\n   - Drinks: There are 2 options (Lemonade, Root Beer).\n   - Desserts: There are 2 options (Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie).\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of distinct possible meals:**\n   - For each entree, Crystal can pair it with any of the 2 drinks and any of the 2 desserts.\n   - Therefore, the total number of distinct meals is the product of the number of choices for each category.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of meals} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting the numbers we have:\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of meals} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 2 = 16\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
